{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b71e-9fa3-7ae0-bf7a-5db7c29ed7af","session_id":"01a1b71e-525f-7f87-9dac-5d469b1f7ff6","message":{"id":"01a1b71e9fa37ae0bf7a5db57050d8de","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test asserts AC-006 is 'planned'. Wait — but does AC-006 have a shard from another task? The merged acs status is derived from shards. T-003 declares AC-006 covered. So the assertion `merged.acs['AC-006'] === 'planned'` fails now.\n\nHmm, but the test at base commit (7f655f7) passed because no shard covered AC-006.\n\nCan we fix this within write_scope? The test asserts AC-006 planned. We can't change the test (not in scope). Alternatives: change T-003.json — but acceptance V-R-2 requires AC-006..072 covered by T-003, and check-traceability expects covered=10.\n\nWait, maybe check-traceability counts covered from test files matching, not from shard. Let's look at check-traceability.mjs and how mergeShards handles multiple shards. Maybe the test picks AC-006 because it's a different assertion — maybe AC-006 is covered by another task already? Let's check test/traceability dir.\n\nActually the review says exactly: V-R-1 and V-R-2 are mutually exclusive under current test. So a design-level conflict. As the dev in round 2, I should check whether design.md has been updated (it hasn't). Then what can I do? My instruction: \"让 acceptance.md 里每一条命令都能通过\". V-R-1 requires check-fast pass, which requires the AC-004 test to pass.\n\nOptions within write_scope:\n1. Make the traceability shard NOT mark AC-006 covered... but V-R-2 requires merged AC-006 = covered. And check-traceability expects covered=10, planned=64.\n\nHmm wait. Where does check-traceability get \"covered\"? Maybe it uses test titles: AC is covered if a test file has `test('[AC-006] ...')`. Let me check.\n\nLet me read check-traceability.mjs and the traceability lib.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"i